3 JOHN

CH1

14
I hope to see you soon and we will speak face to face. Peace to you. The friends greet you. Greet the friends by name.

13
I had many things to write to you but I do not wish to write to you with ink and pen.

12
Demetrius has received a good testimony from everyone and from the truth itself and we also testify and you know that our testimony is true.

11
Beloved do not imitate evil but good. The one who does good is of God the one who does evil has not seen God.

10
Therefore if I come I will call attention to his deeds which he does unjustly accusing us with wicked words and not satisfied with these he himself does not receive the brothers and those who desire to do so he forbids and casts them out of the church.

9
I wrote something to the church but Diotrephes who loves to be first among them does not receive us.

8
Therefore we ought to support such men so that we may be fellow workers with the truth.

7
For they went out for the sake of the name taking nothing from the Gentiles.

6
They have testified to your love before the church and you will do well to send them on their way in a manner worthy of God.

5
Beloved you are acting faithfully in whatever you do for the brothers and this even though they are strangers.

4
I have no greater joy than this to hear of my children walking in the truth.

3
For I rejoiced greatly when brothers came and testified to your truth just as you are walking in truth.

2
Beloved I pray that in all respects you may prosper and be in good health just as your soul prospers.

1
The elder to the beloved Gaius whom I love in truth.
